# Field-identical to rosbag2_interfaces/srv/GetSubscribedTopics, deliberately.
#
# That upstream service exists on the rosbag2 rolling branch but is NOT in any released version:
# apt's rosbag2_interfaces 0.34.0 does not carry it. Depending on it therefore forced every user
# to clone rosbag2 at a pinned commit and compile 22 packages -- roughly forty minutes -- to
# obtain one .srv file, in exchange for source compatibility with clients that cannot exist yet,
# since no released rosbag2 offers the service either.
#
# Defining it here drops that dependency entirely: `apt install ros-rolling-rosbag2` plus a build
# of two small packages. The seven control services we reuse from rosbag2_interfaces (Pause,
# Resume, TogglePaused, IsPaused, Snapshot, SplitBagfile, Stop) ARE in the release, so stock
# compatibility is kept where it actually buys something.
#
# Because the fields match, switching back to the upstream definition later is a one-line change
# once it ships in a release.

---

# Fully qualified names of topics currently subscribed by the recorder.
string[] topics
